  "answer_text": "Here is an overview of **wakehealth.edu** \u2014 the web home of **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfe5 Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist\n\n**Website:** [wakehealth.edu](https://www.wakehealth.edu)\n\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is a nationally recognized, fully integrated academic medical center and health system located in **Winston-Salem, North Carolina**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe8 Clinical System\nThe system is anchored by **Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist Medical Center**, an **885-bed tertiary-care hospital** in Winston-Salem, and includes **Brenner Children's Hospital**, five community hospitals, more than **300 primary and specialty care locations**, and more than **2,700 physicians**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf93 Academic & Research Mission\nOne of its two main components is **Wake Forest University School of Medicine**, a recognized leader in experiential medical education and groundbreaking research. Together, Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist and Wake Forest University School of Medicine serve as the **academic core of Advocate Health**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udd1d Part of Advocate Health\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist is part of **Advocate Health**, the **third-largest nonprofit health system** in the United States. It employs more than **20,000 teammates**, part of Advocate Health's 150,000 teammates.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf0d Community Impact\nAtrium Health Wake Forest Baptist provided a record-setting **$611.2 million in community benefits** during the 2021 fiscal year, which includes unreimbursed care, charity care, education and research, and community health improvement.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe5 Specialties Offered\nSpecialties include **Preventive Care, Specialized Care, Children's Hospital, Comprehensive Cancer Center, Digestive Health Center, Heart Center, Neurosciences, Orthopaedics, Transplantation, Level I Trauma Center, and Urology**.\n\n---\n\nIs there something specific about Wake Health or Atrium Health Wake Forest Baptist you'd like to know more about?",
